Open accuracy issues (reported historically; not yet retested with the updated generator):
- King and queen confusion.
- Bishop and pawn confusion.
- Occasional knight and rook confusion.

Balanced recognition positions, style coverage, milder corruption, and a strict
piece-size floor address possible data causes. They do not establish that these
model errors are fixed. Retraining and real screenshot evaluation remain open.

The earlier generator at 8c16c3decf88d93a5f5497d98ec87b1cef65eeed was reported to
work best with 100 epochs and patience 30; that schedule is now the shared default.
The historical 35-image full-image / refined-search results and reproduction
commands are preserved in README.md under "Historical results and known failures".
The exact checkpoint and full training configuration were not recorded here.

The original small-board-background generation task is implemented and covered
by a rendering/label regression test. Actual trained-model accuracy on those
scenes still needs evaluation. See .todo for the remaining checks.
